// REJECTS: Unsupported connection value type: NoSuchConnection
//
// The ###Connection section is pure island routing: `connection: connectionType
// qualifiedName connectionValue` where connectionType is any `identifier` and the value is
// an opaque brace-balanced blob. The section grammar has no list of connection types and
// cannot have one -- every store extension registers its own.
//
// So the ONLY thing standing between a typo and a silently-loaded connection is the registry
// lookup, and this pins that it happens. It doubles as the packaging canary: if a connection
// type that should exist ever produces this message, the extension is missing from the
// classpath rather than from the grammar.
###Connection
NoSuchConnection fixture::neg::UnknownConnectionType
{
   url: 'model://fixture/person.json';
}
